Summary:
Today’s work focused on implementing the scoring logic for evaluating developer portfolios. I created a utility function in scoring.js to calculate scores based on various factors such as repository activity, total stars, language diversity, and profile completeness. This function processes GitHub user and repository data to generate a structured evaluation score. It serves as a core component for the portfolio analysis system.

Outcomes:
Through this task, I gained a deeper understanding of designing reusable utility functions for business logic. I improved my ability to work with arrays, aggregation methods, and conditional scoring techniques in JavaScript. This implementation makes the evaluation process more systematic and consistent. Overall, it establishes the foundation for a meaningful and data-driven portfolio assessment system.
